      {
        "base": "https://www.wananga.com/feed/rss2",
        "language": null,
        "type": "text/html",
        "value": "<div>\n  <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://irp.cdn-website.com/002b888d/dms3rep/multi/3_Toiora+whanau_Symposium_Web+Banner_2024.jpg\" />\n</div>\n<div>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <span>\n        \n            HE KARERE - AN INVITATION\n           \n      </span>\n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <span>\n        \n            Toiora Wh\u0101nau Symposium \u201cHe Kura te Tangata\u201d\n           \n      </span>\n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <span>\n        \n            He Toiora Tangata, He Toiora Wh\u0101nau\n           \n      </span>\n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <span>\n        \n            11-12 November 2024, Te Ara a T\u0101whaki, Te W\u0101nanga o Raukawa, \u014ctaki\n           \n      </span>\n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <br />\n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <span>\n        \n            \u201cAn intensive 24-hour kaupapa M\u0101ori supervision experience\u201d Haere mai r\u0101 e te iwi ki runga i te kaupapa o te w\u0101 Karanga mai r\u0101! Calling all M\u0101ori practitioners, supervisors and supervisees working in health, education and social services.\n           \n      </span>\n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           Join us here at Te W\u0101nanga o Raukawa for a transformative journey as we share m\u0101tauranga, engage in hauora traditions, and strengthen kaupapa M\u0101ori supervision practices, to enhance the wellbeing of wh\u0101nau, hap\u016b and iwi.\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <br />\n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           The symposium theme is \u201cHe kura te tangata\u201d translated as \u2018the people prospered\u2019, through his/her leadership and administration. This underlines the vital role that skilled kaupapa M\u0101ori supervisors play in fostering the wellbeing of practitioners. The symposium will feature hauora traditions, speakers and panel discussions in a safe space where you can be recharged and engage in critical discussions that empower wh\u0101nau, hap\u016b and iwi.\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <br />\n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           Keynote speaker: Dr. Meihana Durie\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <br />\n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           Kaupapa M\u0101ori models of supervision presented by: Wheturangi Walsh-Tapiata, Maree Tukukino, Dr. Moana Eruera, Dr. Leland Ruwhiu, Tracey Robinson and Poutuarongo Toiora Wh\u0101nau graduates. Hauora traditions: instructed by Rita Tupe, Maudy Tupe, Mate Tihema, Kim Savage, Robbie Richardson, Hinepuororangi Winiata, Tracey Patete, Ezra Bevan, Brian Climie, Kelly-Anne Ngatai, Tipi Wehipeihana and Tasha Webby.\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n</div>\n<div>\n  <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://irp.cdn-website.com/002b888d/dms3rep/multi/Toiora+Wha-nau+Images-3.jpg\" />\n</div>\n<div>\n  <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://irp.cdn-website.com/002b888d/dms3rep/multi/Toiora+Wha-nau+Images-2.jpg\" />\n</div>\n<div>\n  <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://irp.cdn-website.com/002b888d/dms3rep/multi/Toiora+Wha-nau+Images.jpg\" />\n</div>"
      }
    ],
